{
  "id": "p300",
  "term": "P300",
  "definition": "P300 is a positive brain-response signal seen on EEG about 300 milliseconds after a person notices an expected target that appears rarely and unpredictably. In psychology and brain-computer interface work, it is treated as one type of event-related potential linked to detecting meaningful target stimuli.",
